-- title:
--   Drinfeld deformation rings are regular of dimension two
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $W_0$ a complete discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and which is equipped with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. (for the trivial ideal) its $q$-th iterate series `F₀.nthSeries q` equals a unit power series times `F₀.drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`. Let $F_u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[X]]$ whose base change along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ (i.e. the coefficientwise image of its defining two-variable series) is $F_0$, and assume the linear coefficient of the $q$-th coefficient of `Fu.nthSeries q` is congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$. Let $R$ be a noetherian local $W_0$-algebra, complete for its maximal-adic topology, with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ with kernel $\mathfrak{m}_R$ agreeing with $\mathrm{res}_0$ on $W_0$, and let $F$ be a commutative formal group law over $R$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_R$ is $F_0$, together with $x_0, x_1 \in \mathfrak{m}_R$ such that `F.nthSeries q` is a unit times `F.drinfeldDivisor q x₀ x₁` in the $\mathfrak{m}_R$-adic sense. Assume finally that $R$ is universal in the following rigidified sense: for every artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_T$ onto $k$ with kernel $\mathfrak{m}_T$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, every commutative formal group law $G$ over $T$ lifting $F_0$ and every $y_0, y_1 \in \mathfrak{m}_T$ forming such a Drinfeld datum for $G$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : R \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_R$ for which the base change $F'$ of $F$ along $\varphi$ admits an isomorphism $\psi$ of formal group laws to $G$ whose series has residues $\delta_{n,1}$ and which carries $\varphi(x_0), \varphi(x_1)$ to $y_0, y_1$ under $\mathfrak{m}_T$-adic evaluation. Then $R$ is a regular local ring and $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} R = 2$.
--
--   This is Drinfeld's regularity theorem for the deformation space of a height-two formal group with Drinfeld level-$q$ structure: the pro-representing ring is regular of dimension two. It is the input to the hypersurface presentation of such deformation rings, and is used in the analysis of the adic completions of modular curves with full level structure (integrality and reducedness statements there).
